1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
You live abroad, and you're building
a house back home.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,500
Every month you send money,
and you get photos on your phone.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:12,000
Were they taken on your plot?
This week?

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Plotwatch replaces trust with evidence.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,500
Ada, the funder, creates a project from a template,
with its stages and budget,

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:26,500
and invites her site manager.

7
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:30,000
Joseph joins with the code.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
On the plot, Joseph localizes the site
with his phone's GPS.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Ada checks it on the map
and sets the boundary.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,500
Now Joseph photographs the work,
only through the app's camera, never the gallery.

11
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:51,000
Seconds later it appears on Ada's screen,
live, and it's verified.

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,000
The server checked the position against the boundary,
the time against its own clock, and the photo's fingerprint.

13
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000
A photo taken eighty metres away?
Unverified, and Plotwatch says exactly why.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,000
When every required photo is in,
Joseph submits the stage.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Ada is notified at once,
reviews the evidence and approves.

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Plotwatch offers to record the next payment.

17
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Every payment and expense lands in a shared ledger,
with receipt photos.

18
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Entries are never edited, only reversed.

19
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:45,000
And Plotwatch flags money
that isn't backed by receipts yet.

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,500
Plotwatch is built with Flutter and Serverpod:
live streams, scheduled tasks,

21
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:55,000
verified uploads and authentication,
on Serverpod Cloud.

22
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Try it at plotwatch.serverpod.space.
